  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promote multi-stakeholder approach to digital technology development</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Digital transformation over the years has continuously affected how people live, work, function in their societies. It also has impacted the how government function and operate. Digital transformation, including artificial intelligence (AI) adoption, has become one of the highest priorities for public organizations. 

Harnessing the opportunities offered by the digital innovation and transformation while addressing the ethical challenges embedded in the development and use of digital technologies including Artificial Intelligence would be pursued within the 42 C5 programmes. To achieve this, UNESCO will strengthen knowledge of judicial actors and partners to promote discussion around AI&#x2019;s application and impact on the rule of law, the benefits of digital transformation towards the achievement of fair, inclusive, human centric and diverse digital transformation. This would also stimulate technical dialogues towards the enactment of policies and good practices into the ecosystem.</narrative>
  </description>
